        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "{\"output\":\"# Service component\\n\\nSecure get_document(connection, tenant, owner, document_id) and list_documents in src/service.py. Only documents matching both tenant and owner and having deleted_at IS NULL are accessible. get_document returns None for any unavailable ID without distinguishing cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted records. Lists return dictionaries ordered by id, and no deletion metadata. All queries use bound parameters, including names containing quotes. Keep result fields id, title and body unchanged. Start in src/service.py and src/repository.py.\\n\\nRun `python3 checks/public.py` from the project root. Implementation belongs in src/. Add checks under checks/.\\n======\\nfrom .repository import find, listing\\n\\ndef get_document(connection, tenant, owner, document_id):\\n    return find(connection, document_id)\\n\\ndef list_documents(connection, tenant, owner):\\n    return listing(connection, owner)\\n======\\ndef initialize(connection):\\n    connection.execute(\\\"CREATE TABLE documents(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, tenant TEXT, owner TEXT, title TEXT, body TEXT, deleted_at TEXT)\\\")\\n    connection.commit()\\n\\ndef decode(row):\\n    return {\\\"id\\\": row[0], \\\"title\\\": row[1], \\\"body\\\": row[2]}\\n\\ndef find(connection, document_id):\\n    row = connection.execute(\\\"SELECT id, title, body FROM documents WHERE id=?\\\", (document_id,)).fetchone()\\n    return None if row is None else decode(row)\\n\\ndef listing(connection, owner):\\n    return [decode(row) for row in connection.execute(\\\"SELECT id, title, body FROM documents WHERE owner=? ORDER BY id\\\", (owner,))]\\n======\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
